cm2n+@andrew.cmu.edu (Christopher A. Maloney) writes:
--- argues that magical objects affect character overall, no matter where
--- worn

I accept that argument, since overall, I like the game and magical objects
are an important part of the game.  Changing those would make it a very
different (and I think less interesting) game.  What concerns me is that
it is possible to go overboard with magical items.  I hope that Mr. Hairston
is not serious about his "badge of clumsiness" idea.  The game is arbitrary
enough as it is and it is only too easy to have your fortunes take a turn
for the worse quickly in this game ...

However, there still remains the question of what the dexterity stat is for.
When I put those gloves on, my dexterity stat did not change, but my
dexterity went down drastically!  Is this a bug or a feature?  I realize
that higher dexterity means you can carry more items and vice versa, but
isn't dexterity also related to clumsiness?

